### 1. Task outcome (short version):
Screened 100 studies against the systematic review protocol for "Effects of total fat intake on body weight." Results: 
13 studies INCLUDED, 87 studies EXCLUDED. Key inclusion criteria were: RCT or cohort design, adults/children ≥24 months,
lower fat vs usual/moderate fat diet WITHOUT weight loss intention, not multifactorial, and weight/fatness measured 
after ≥6 months.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):

**SUMMARY STATISTICS:**
- Total studies screened: 100
- Studies included: 13 (13%)
- Studies excluded: 87 (87%)

**INCLUDED STUDIES (13):**

| Study # | Title | Rationale |
|---------|-------|-----------|
| 1 | The impact for the guidelines for a healthy diet of the Netherlands Nutrition Council on total and high density 
lipoprotein cholesterol in hypercholesterolemic free living men | RCT, 26-week follow-up, weight measured, primary focus
on cholesterol not weight loss |
| 2 | A randomised controlled trial of the effect of low fat diet advice on dietary response in insulin independent 
diabetic women | RCT, 6-month follow-up, weight measured, weight loss appears secondary |
| 4 | Long term metabolic effects of two dietary methods of treating hyperlipidaemia | RCT, 6-month follow-up, BMI 
measured, exclusion of BMI>30 suggests weight maintenance |
| 6 | Effects of a diet higher in carbohydrate/lower in fat versus lower in carbohydrate/higher in monounsaturated fat 
on postmeal triglyceride concentrations and other cardiovascular risk factors in type 1 diabetes | RCT, eucaloric 
design, 6-month follow-up, BMI measured |
| 9 | A randomized controlled trial of a public health nurse directed treatment program for rural patients with high 
blood cholesterol | RCT, 12-month follow-up, weight measured, primary focus on cholesterol |
| 10 | The Anti‐Coronary Club: 1957‐1972 | Historical dietary intervention, long-term follow-up, weight reduction not 
primary intention |
| 11 | Diet, lipoprotiens and progression of coronary atherosclerosis: the Leiden intervention trial | RCT, 24-month 
follow-up, weight measured, primary focus on coronary lesions |
| 15 | Long‐term effect of nutritional counseling: a study in family medicine | RCT, 17-year follow-up, dietary fat 
intake assessed |
| 16 | A low‐fat vegan diet and a conventional diabetes diet in the treatment of type 2 diabetes: a randomized, 
controlled, 74‐wk clinical trial | RCT, 74-week follow-up, weight measured, primary focus on glycemic control |
| 33 | Long‐term effects of ad libitum low‐fat, high‐carbohydrate diets on body weight and serum lipids in overweight 
subjects with metabolic syndrome | RCT, ad libitum feeding (no calorie restriction), 6-month follow-up |
| 34 | Randomized controlled trial of changes in dietary carbohydrate/fat ratio and simple vs complex carbohydrates on 
body weight and blood lipids: the CARMEN study | RCT, 6-month follow-up, weight measured, primary focus on macronutrient
composition |
| 35 | Micronutrient intake in overweight subjects is not deficient on and ad libitum fat‐reduced, high‐simple 
carbohydrate diet | RCT, ad libitum fat-reduced diet, 6-month follow-up |
| 94 | Long‐term effects of nutrition with fat‐reduced foods on energy consumption and body weight | RCT, ad libitum 
fat-reduced foods, 6-month follow-up |

**EXCLUSION CATEGORIES (87 studies):**

1. **Weight loss was primary intention (38 studies):** Studies 18, 19, 24, 27, 29, 31, 32, 38, 39, 41, 44, 45, 46, 47, 
