  Rationale: RCT comparing tailored intervention promoting lower fat intake vs no materials. Assessed fat intake change.
However, unclear if weight was measured at 6+ months and whether weight reduction was intended. Need to check if this 
meets all criteria.

Study 246: An eight‐month controlled study of a low‐fat high‐fibre diet: effects on blood lipids and blood pressure in 
healthy young subjects
  Rationale: RCT comparing low-fat diet (<30% energy from fat) vs habitual diet (36% fat) in healthy young adults. 
8-month follow-up (>6 months). Body weight measured monthly. No explicit intention to reduce weight stated - diet 
corresponds to Nordic Nutrition Recommendations.

